WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.853
An agent can finish with the wrong record.

00:00:03.853 --> 00:00:10.000
Richard Wolff's AI-assisted adaptation
verifies before publication.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.353
A fixed synthetic request binds identity
and exact generated bytes.

00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:21.000
Verification must pass before the sink
publishes.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.814
The first run creates the record.

00:00:23.814 --> 00:00:27.140
Final readback checks the landed bytes.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:32.000
A separate verifier reopens and hashes the
physical file.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.273
The sink uses atomic, no-overwrite
publication.

00:00:36.273 --> 00:00:42.364
Identical bytes are reused; changed bytes
get a hash-named variant.

00:00:42.364 --> 00:00:45.000
The original stays unchanged.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.455
Now supply the wrong subject identity.

00:00:48.455 --> 00:00:54.000
Collection refuses, leaving the existing
artifacts unchanged.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.444
A separate rehearsal changes its own
generated file.

00:00:58.444 --> 00:01:04.000
Physical verification detects the changed
bytes and rejects them.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.956
The MCP-shaped wrapper is an in-process
mock.

00:01:06.956 --> 00:01:08.861
It authenticates no provider.

00:01:08.861 --> 00:01:13.000
Hashes check observed bytes, not their
origin or future safety.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.742
Make success depend on verified bytes.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:20.000
Inspect sample and runtime in Verified
Artifact Collection.
